<header class="main-header">
  <div class="series-title">Likutay Halachos &middot; Choshen Mishpat</div>
  <h1>Hilchos Da&rsquo;yonim 3</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">Laws of Judges &mdash; 3</div>
</header>

<div class="verse-block">
  Based on the teaching <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;T&rsquo;homos y&rsquo;chasyumu&rdquo;</span> in Likutay [Moharan] I, Siman 9
  <span class="source-ref">See there what is explained on the verse &ldquo;A <em>tzohar</em> you shall make for the <em>taivah</em> etc.&rdquo; <span class="source">(Genesis 6:16)</span></span>
</div>

<!-- ====== OS 1 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 1</div>

<p>
Based on the teaching <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;T&rsquo;homos y&rsquo;chasyumu&rdquo;</span> [&ldquo;The depths covered them&rdquo;] in Likutay [Moharan] I, Siman 9. See there what is explained on the verse: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;A <em>tzohar</em> [light/window] you shall make for the <em>taivah</em> [ark] etc.&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 6:16)</span>. And the general principle [is that] when a person stands to pray, then alien thoughts and <span class="key-term">k&rsquo;lipos</span> <span class="key-term-def">[husks of impurity]</span> come and surround him, and he remains in darkness and cannot pray etc. And in truth there are many openings within the darkness through which to exit from there etc., but the person is blind and does not know how to find the opening. And through <span class="key-term">emes</span> <span class="key-term-def">[truth]</span> he merits to find the opening, for the essential light that illuminates is the Holy One, Blessed is He, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Hashem is my light and my salvation&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 27:1)</span>. And through <span class="key-term">sheker</span> <span class="key-term-def">[falsehood]</span> one drives away the Holy One, Blessed is He, etc. But through truth, the Holy One, Blessed is He, dwells with him etc. And when the Holy One, Blessed is He, is with him, He illuminates for him how to exit from the darkness that prevents him in his prayer, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Hashem is my light.&rdquo;</span>
</p>

<p>
And this is the meaning of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;A <em>tzohar</em> you shall make for the <em>taivah</em> etc.&rdquo;</span> And it all depends upon the magnitude of the truth etc. And then: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And the opening of the <em>taivah</em> you shall place at its side&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 6:16)</span>. That is, the <em>taivah</em> [word] that goes forth in truth &mdash; it will set for you an opening in the darkness in which you are trapped etc. And through exiting from within the darkness and praying well, through this he rectifies <span class="scripture">&ldquo;lower, second, and third [stories]&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 6:16)</span> &mdash; that is, the <span class="key-term">olam hashofel</span> <span class="key-term-def">[lower world]</span>, the <span class="key-term">olam hakochavim</span> <span class="key-term-def">[world of the stars]</span>, and the <span class="key-term">olam hasaichel</span> <span class="key-term-def">[world of the intellect]</span> etc. See there.
</p>

<div class="word-note">
<strong>Word-play:</strong> The word <em>taivah</em> (תיבה) means both &ldquo;ark&rdquo; (as in Noach&rsquo;s ark) and &ldquo;word&rdquo; (as in a word of prayer). <em>Tzohar</em> (צהר) means both &ldquo;window/skylight&rdquo; and &ldquo;radiance/light.&rdquo; Thus: &ldquo;Make a <em>tzohar</em> for the <em>taivah</em>&rdquo; = &ldquo;Make a radiance/light for the word [of prayer].&rdquo; The three stories of the ark (lower, second, third) correspond to the three worlds sustained through proper prayer.
</div>

<!-- ====== OS 2 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 2</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of three da&rsquo;yonim [judges], for the essential rectification of <span class="key-term">mishpat tzedek</span> <span class="key-term-def">[righteous judgment]</span> is <span class="key-term">emes</span> [truth], for it is impossible to clarify the judgment except through truth. For when the two litigants come to be judged and contradict one another regarding a monetary matter &mdash; this is the aspect of the intensification of the darkness exceedingly, for the <span class="key-term">sheker</span> [falsehood] is darkness. And especially since the essence of their denial is on account of money &mdash; it emerges that they have fallen into the <span class="key-term">ta&rsquo;avas mamon</span> <span class="key-term-def">[lust for money]</span> to the point that one wishes to oppress and rob his fellow, which is the essential lust for money. And the lust for money is the aspect of darkness, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;He has set me in darkness&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Lamentations 3:6)</span>, as is well-explained in the teaching <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;Tzivisa Tzedek&rdquo;</span> etc., see there (Siman 23), that the lust for money is a very great darkness, the aspect of <span class="aramaic">anpin chashochin</span> <span class="key-term-def">[dark faces]</span> &mdash; idolatry that is comprised of all the seventy nations.
</p>

<p>
It emerges that all types of darkness, which is the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achara</span> [Other Side] and the idolatry &mdash; all the seventy <span class="aramaic">anpin chashochin</span> [dark faces] &mdash; are all included in the lust for money, which is the aspect of falsehood, as is explained there. And therefore the judge who sits to judge &mdash; it is as if <span class="key-term">Gehinnom</span> <span class="key-term-def">[purgatory]</span> is open beneath him, as our Sages of blessed memory said <span class="source">(Yevamos 109b)</span>, for the intensity of the darkness intensifies then, which is the aspect of the darkness of <span class="key-term">Gehinnom</span> where the essential darkness and shadow of death reside &mdash; since one wishes to rob his fellow of money, which is the aspect of the sin of the Generation of the Flood, whose decree was sealed on account of robbery, as our Sages of blessed memory said <span class="source">(Sanhedrin 108a)</span>.
</p>

<p>
And therefore it is in truth exceedingly, exceedingly difficult to clarify a righteous judgment. And therefore the judge cannot clarify the judgment except through truth &mdash; for the essential thing is the truth. That is, the judge should look only at the truth. And there should be in his heart no aspect of bias or inclination, G-d forbid, to any side of the sides, and both [litigants] should be equal in his eyes, and he should look with the eye of truth to its truth. And then, through the magnitude of the truth of the judge &mdash; and truth is the light of Hashem Yisborach Himself &mdash; then it will be fulfilled: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;G-d stands in the congregation of the Mighty; in the midst of the judges He judges&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 82:1)</span>. And then Hashem Yisborach, Who is the very essence of truth, Who is the illuminating light, will illuminate his eyes. And through this the judge will merit to clarify the righteous judgment from within the great darkness, and to be saved from the <span class="key-term">Gehinnom</span> &mdash; which is the great darkness that surrounded him through the falsehood of the darkness of the lust for money, as above. For it is impossible to be saved from all this except through truth, which is the light of Hashem Yisborach Himself, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;G-d stands in the congregation of the Mighty,&rdquo;</span> as above.
</p>

<p>
For without truth it is impossible to clarify any judgment, for there are many distinctions, too numerous to count. And they are <span class="scripture">&ldquo;like mountains hanging by a hair&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Chagigah 1:8)</span>. And also there is a fraudulent case, and it is impossible for the judge not to stumble in the matter of judgment except through truth, which is the light of Hashem Yisborach, which illuminates his eyes and he merits to judge righteously.
</p>

<p>
And this is the aspect of the greatness of the prohibition of bribery: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;For the bribe will blind etc.&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 23:8)</span> &mdash; <span class="precise">&ldquo;will blind,&rdquo; specifically</span>. That is, the aspect of the great darkness mentioned above, which intensifies even more through the lust for money &mdash; that is, bribery &mdash; in which case it is impossible in any manner to judge righteously. And therefore it is forbidden to take a bribe even to acquit the innocent etc., as our Sages of blessed memory said <span class="source">(Kesubos 105a)</span>, for it is impossible in any manner to judge righteously when one takes a bribe, for then he has no truth, for the darkness intensifies exceedingly etc., as above. For it is impossible to exit from this great darkness except through the truth &mdash; that the judge should have great truth and should look only at the truth without any falsehood and without any deviousness whatsoever.
</p>

<p>
And this is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;men of truth, haters of monetary gain&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 18:21)</span>, regarding which the judges are especially warned, for &ldquo;truth&rdquo; and &ldquo;haters of monetary gain&rdquo; are [both] the aspect of truth, for the lust for money is the aspect of darkness, the aspect of falsehood, as explained in the teaching <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;Tzivisa Tzedek&rdquo;</span> mentioned above. It emerges that the essential rectification of the judgment of the da&rsquo;yonim is truth.
</p>

<p>
And therefore there must be <strong>three</strong> da&rsquo;yonim, for through truth &mdash; through which one merits to pray &mdash; through this one merits to sustain all the three worlds, which are the lower world, the world of the stars, and the world of the angels &mdash; which are the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;lower, second, and third [stories] you shall make it&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 6:16)</span>, as above. And this is the aspect of three da&rsquo;yonim, who are the aspect of three lines of truth, the aspect of three prayers per day, which sustain all the three worlds, as above. For the essential sustenance of all the worlds is truth, which is the aspect of the three da&rsquo;yonim, whose essential warning is [regarding] truth, as above.
</p>

<p>
And this is what our Sages of blessed memory said <span class="source">(Shabbos 10a)</span>: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Whoever judges a judgment of truth to its truth becomes as if he became a partner with the Holy One, Blessed is He, in the work of Creation.&rdquo;</span> That is, as above &mdash; for through a judgment of truth to its truth, where he looks only at the truth to its truth, through this he sustains all of the work of Creation, which is the generality of the three worlds mentioned above. And behold, he is a partner with the Holy One, Blessed is He, in the work of Creation, as above.
</p>

<!-- ====== OS 3 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 3</div>

<p>
It emerges that a judgment of truth is the aspect of the rectification of prayer, whose essential rectification is through truth, as above. And this is what our Sages of blessed memory said: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Why is the section of [civil] laws juxtaposed to the section of the altar? To tell you that you should place the judges near the altar&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Sanhedrin 7b)</span>. For the altar, where they offer <span class="key-term">korbanos</span> <span class="key-term-def">[sacrifices]</span>, is the aspect of <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> [prayer], which atones like sacrifices, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And I will gladden them in My house of prayer; their burnt-offerings and their sacrifices shall be accepted upon My altar etc.&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Isaiah 56:7)</span>. And therefore the da&rsquo;yonim need to sit near the altar, for the essential rectification of prayer, which is the aspect of sacrifices, is through truth, which is the aspect of truthful judges, as above.
</p>

<!-- ====== OS 4 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 4</div>

<p>
And therefore the essential judges from the Torah are <span class="key-term">mumchin us&rsquo;muchin</span> <span class="key-term-def">[experts and ordained]</span> in <span class="key-term">Eretz Yisroel</span> <span class="precise">specifically</span>. For the essential rectification of prayer is in Eretz Yisroel, as is explained there in the aforementioned teaching. For there, in Eretz Yisroel, is the essential truth, which is the rectification of prayer, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;A <em>tzohar</em> you shall make for the <em>taivah</em>&rdquo;</span> mentioned above, which illuminates and saves from the waters of the Flood, which are the darkness that surrounds, G-d forbid. For Eretz Yisroel is <span class="scripture">&ldquo;a land that was not rained upon in the day of wrath&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Yechezkel 22:24)</span>, for in Eretz Yisroel the Flood did not occur, as our Sages of blessed memory said <span class="source">(Zevachim 113a)</span>. For there is the essential truth, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Yaakov</span>, as Rabbainu of blessed memory wrote in the teaching <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;Va&rsquo;achaltem achol v&rsquo;savo&rsquo;a&rdquo;</span> (Siman 47), see there.
</p>

<!-- ====== OS 5 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 5</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of the court not concerning itself except for the value of a <span class="key-term">p&rsquo;rutah</span> [smallest coin]. For it is brought there in the aforementioned teaching, regarding the words of our Sages of blessed memory: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;The son of Dovid will not come until the <em>p&rsquo;rutah</em> ceases from the purse&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Sanhedrin 97a)</span> &mdash; that <span class="key-term">p&rsquo;rutah</span> is the aspect of the angel <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;dif&rsquo;ritah sif&rsquo;vasav&rdquo;</span> <span class="key-term-def">[whose lips move/separate]</span>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">emunah</span>, <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> [faith, prayer] etc., see there. And therefore the essential measure of theft is the value of a <span class="key-term">p&rsquo;rutah</span>, for one must conduct business dealings with <span class="key-term">emunah</span> [faithfulness] &mdash; <span class="precise">&ldquo;with <em>emunah</em>,&rdquo; specifically</span>. That is, one must be exceedingly careful not to rob his fellow, for the essential <span class="key-term">emunah</span> depends upon money. That is, when one breaks the lust for money, this is the essential <span class="key-term">emunah</span> in its completeness, as Rabbainu of blessed memory wrote there in the teaching <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;Tzivisa Tzedek Aidosecha V&rsquo;emunah M&rsquo;od&rdquo;</span>. And <span class="key-term">emunah</span> is the aspect of <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">p&rsquo;rutah</span>, as above.
</p>

<p>
And therefore the measure of theft &mdash; which is the lust for money, the blemish of <span class="key-term">emunah</span> &mdash; is the value of a <span class="key-term">p&rsquo;rutah</span>. And therefore the essential sitting of the da&rsquo;yonim is on account of the value of a <span class="key-term">p&rsquo;rutah</span>, for the sitting of the da&rsquo;yonim is in order to clarify the judgment of truth, which is the aspect of the rectification of prayer, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">emunah</span>, as above &mdash; in order to extract the <span class="key-term">p&rsquo;rutah</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">emunah</span>/<span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span>, from the hand of the oppressor who wishes to blemish the <span class="key-term">emunah</span> through the lust for money, as above.
</p>

<p>
And therefore one must give <span class="key-term">tz&rsquo;dakah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[charity]</span> before praying, as our Sages of blessed memory said <span class="source">(Bava Basra 10a)</span>, for <span class="key-term">tz&rsquo;dakah</span> is the aspect of breaking the lust for money, as Rabbainu of blessed memory wrote in the teaching that begins <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;L&rsquo;hamshich hashgachah sh&rsquo;laimah&rdquo;</span> etc. (Siman 13). And when one breaks the lust for money, then the <span class="key-term">emunah</span> is completed, as above, which is the essential rectification of prayer, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">emunah</span>, as above. And therefore the measure of <span class="key-term">tz&rsquo;dakah</span> is also a <span class="key-term">p&rsquo;rutah</span>, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">p&rsquo;rutah</span> mentioned above, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">emunah</span>/<span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span>, as above.
</p>

<!-- ====== OS 6 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 6</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of two witnesses, who have trustworthiness [<em>ne&rsquo;emanus</em> &mdash; note the root shared with <em>emunah</em>] and they clarify the truth &mdash; which of the two litigants claims truth &mdash; as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;By the mouth of two witnesses a matter shall be established&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 19:15)</span>.
</p>

<p>
And this is the aspect of the secret of the <span class="key-term">ibbur</span> <span class="key-term-def">[intercalation/leap year]</span> that was given over to the <span class="key-term">bais din</span> to intercalate years and to establish new months. And they intercalate Adar and add a month to the twelve months, and the year becomes sometimes thirteen months, in order to equalize the solar years with the lunar months so that the <span class="key-term">Sholosh Regolim</span> [Three Festivals] should be in their [proper] time, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Guard the month of spring etc.&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 16:1)</span>, as our Sages of blessed memory said.
</p>

<p>
For it is explained in the teaching <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;T&rsquo;homos y&rsquo;chasyumu&rdquo;</span> mentioned above that truth is the essential rectification of prayer, through which one sees the openings to exit from within the great darkness and the <span class="key-term">k&rsquo;lipos</span> that surround a person at the time of prayer, so that he cannot pray because of them. And there is no remedy for this except through truth &mdash; that a person must strengthen himself and exert himself with all his might to bring forth the utterance from his mouth in truth, in whatever capacity he can, even if he cannot pray at all. At the very least, let him say the word from his mouth in truth, with complete simplicity, so long as it is in truth. And then the word of truth will illuminate for him to exit from within the darkness, and he will be able to pray well etc., as is explained there.
</p>

<p>
And it is brought there that truth has two aspects. For there are those whose speech is complete truth to its truth, and then their utterance is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">precious stone</span> [<em>even tov</em>] that illuminates on its own etc. And there are those whose utterance is truth, but it is not so completely clear truth, and then their speech is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span> [<em>chalon</em>] &mdash; that is, another can illuminate through it. For the difference between a precious stone and a window is that a window has no light of its own; rather, through it the light enters. But when there is no light [outside], it does not illuminate. But a precious stone, even when there is no light from outside, illuminates on its own.
</p>

<p>
So too, there are people whose speech is the very essence of truth, the aspect of a precious stone. And there are those whose truth is less refined &mdash; the aspect of a window, through which the tzadik of truth illuminates. And these two aspects are the aspect of two witnesses &mdash; for they are called <span class="scripture">&ldquo;witnesses&rdquo;</span> because they are the aspect of truth, as is explained there, that truth is called <span class="scripture">&ldquo;testimony&rdquo;</span> [<em>aidus</em>] in many places, as in: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;The testimony of Hashem is faithful&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 19:8)</span>. And the two witnesses are the aspect of the two types of truth &mdash; the precious stone and the window &mdash; for through both of them the truth is clarified.
</p>

<div class="word-note">
<strong>Conceptual note:</strong> The two levels of truth &mdash; <em>even tov</em> (precious stone = self-illuminating truth) and <em>chalon</em> (window = truth that transmits light from another source) &mdash; map onto many pairs: sun and moon, Torah and prayer, the tzadik and the ordinary person, and here &mdash; the two witnesses whose testimony establishes the facts. Both types are needed: the complete truth of the Torah/tzadik, and the sincere-but-imperfect truth of the person who draws close to it.
</div>

<p>
And in Siman 112, where this matter is also repeated on the verse <span class="scripture">&ldquo;A light shall you make for the ark&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 6:16)</span>, with a bit of additional explanation. And everything is according to the greatness of the truth etc. For the essential longing of Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> is only for truth etc. And every person must connect his prayer to the <span class="key-term">Tzadik</span> of the generation, and the <span class="key-term">Tzadik</span> knows how to direct the gates and to elevate each and every prayer to the gate that pertains to it. For every <span class="key-term">Tzadik</span> is the aspect of Moshe&ndash;Moshiach etc., and Moshiach is comprised of all the prayers etc.
</p>

<p>
For there are twelve tribes corresponding to twelve <span class="key-term">mazalos</span> <span class="key-term-def">[constellations]</span>. And each and every tribe has a unique formulation [of prayer] and has a unique gate through which its prayer enters. And each tribe arouses through its prayer the power of its <span class="key-term">mazal</span> among the twelve <span class="key-term">mazalos</span>, and the <span class="key-term">mazal</span> illuminates below and causes the growth to flourish etc. And this is the aspect of: <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;A person&rsquo;s livelihood is as difficult as the splitting of the Sea of Reeds, and his match is difficult&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">(Pesachim 118a, Sotah 2a)</span> &mdash; for the Sea of Reeds was split into twelve parts corresponding to the twelve tribes etc.
</p>

<p>
And this is the meaning of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;They guarded His testimonies and the statute He gave them&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 99:7)</span>. <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Testimony&rdquo;</span> &mdash; this is prayer, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;The tribes of Yah, a testimony etc., to give thanks to the Name of Hashem&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">(Psalms 122:4)</span>. For in prayer we testify to His unity. And according to the prayer, so one merits livelihood and to find one&rsquo;s match etc.; see there all of this well.
</p>

<!-- ====== OS 7 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 7</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of the secret of the <span class="key-term">ibbur</span> [intercalation]. They intercalate the year in order to equalize the moon with the sun, which is the aspect of filling the blemish of the moon so that the light of the moon should be like the light of the sun. For the essential illuminating light of the sun and the moon &mdash; which were given to illuminate upon the earth, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And they shall be for luminaries, and for signs, and for festivals etc.&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 1:14)</span> &mdash; the essential light of theirs is truth, which is the essential illuminating light, as above. And therefore they are two luminaries, the sun and moon &mdash; this is the aspect of the two aspects mentioned above, which are the aspects of the precious stone and the window. For the precious stone illuminates on its own, and the window does not illuminate on its own, rather it receives the light from another. And this is the aspect of sun and moon, which are the aspects of <span class="aramaic">ispaklaryah d&rsquo;nahara mi&rsquo;garmah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[a lens that shines of its own]</span> &mdash; which is the sun, which illuminates on its own, the aspect of the precious stone mentioned above &mdash; and the moon, which is the aspect of <span class="aramaic">ispaklaryah d&rsquo;lo nahara mi&rsquo;garmah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[a lens that does not shine of its own]</span>, rather only what it receives from the sun &mdash; which is the aspect of a window that does not illuminate on its own, but only what it receives from another, as above.
</p>

<p>
And this is the aspect of the secret of the diminution of the moon, from which the essential hold of the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achara</span> [Other Side] and the <span class="key-term">k&rsquo;lipos</span> [husks] and the <span class="key-term">yaitzer hara</span> <span class="key-term-def">[evil inclination]</span> [derive]. And from there all sins and all blemishes that come through the evil inclination, which takes hold from there, descend and come. And the essence of our service all the days of the world is to rectify this &mdash; to rectify the blemish of the moon so that there should be no diminution in it, and the light of the moon should be like the light of the sun, as is known. For the sun and moon were created equal, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;The two great luminaries&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 1:16)</span>. But because of the complaint of the moon, which said: &ldquo;It is impossible for two kings to use one crown,&rdquo; therefore it was diminished <span class="source">(Chullin 60b)</span>. For in truth, the essential creation was only for the sake of truth, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;In the beginning G-d created the heavens and the earth&rdquo;</span> &mdash; and our Sages of blessed memory said: <strong><em>bara Elokim es</em></strong> &mdash; the final letters [of these three words] spell <strong><em>emes</em></strong> [truth] <span class="source">(Bereishis Rabbah)</span>.
</p>

<div class="word-note">
<strong>Root / letter play:</strong> The words בָּרָ֣א אֱלֹקִ֑ים אֵ֥ת (bara Elokim es) end in the letters א-ם-ת &mdash; spelling <em>emes</em> (truth). This hints that the entire purpose of Creation is truth, and that when truth is blemished (through the moon&rsquo;s complaint, through falsehood), the light diminishes and the forces of darkness gain a hold.
</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of the secret of <span class="key-term">ibbur</span> <span class="key-term-def">[intercalation]</span>: that they intercalate the year in order to equalize the moon with the sun. For this is the aspect of filling the blemish of the moon, so that the light of the moon should be like the light of the sun. For the essential illuminating light of the sun and the moon &mdash; which were given to illuminate upon the earth, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And they shall be for luminaries and for signs and for seasons&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">(Genesis 1:14)</span> &mdash; their essential light is <span class="key-term">emes</span>, which is the essential illuminating light, as above. And therefore they are two luminaries, the sun and the moon &mdash; this is the aspect of the two aforementioned aspects, which are the aspects of a precious stone and a window. For a precious stone illuminates on its own, and a window does not illuminate on its own but rather receives the light from another. This is the aspect of the sun and the moon, which are the aspects of an <span class="aramaic">ispaklaryah d&rsquo;nahara mi&rsquo;garma</span> <span class="key-term-def">[a lens that shines of its own]</span> &mdash; which is the sun, which illuminates on its own, the aspect of the precious stone mentioned above. And the moon is the aspect of an <span class="aramaic">ispaklaryah d&rsquo;lo nahara mi&rsquo;garma</span> <span class="key-term-def">[a lens that does not shine of its own]</span> at all, but only what it receives from the sun &mdash; which is the aspect of a window, which does not illuminate on its own, but only what it receives from another, as above.
</p>

<p>
And this is the aspect of the secret of <span class="key-term">mi&rsquo;ut hayareach</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the diminution of the moon]</span>, from which derives the essential hold of the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achara</span> and the <span class="key-term">k&rsquo;lipos</span> and the <span class="key-term">Yetzer HaRa</span>. And from there descend and come all the sins and all the blemishes that come through the <span class="key-term">Yetzer HaRa</span>, which takes hold from there. And our essential service, all the days of the world, is to rectify this &mdash; to rectify the blemish of the moon so that there should be no diminution in it, and the light of the moon should be like the light of the sun, as is known.
</p>

<p>
For the sun and moon were created equal, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;the two great luminaries&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 1:16)</span>. But because of the complaint of the moon, which said: <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;It is impossible for two kings to use one crown,&rdquo;</span> therefore it was diminished <span class="source">(Chullin 60b)</span>. For in truth, the essential Creation was only for the sake of truth, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;In the beginning G-d created the heavens and the earth&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 1:1)</span>. And our Sages, of blessed memory, said: <em>Bara Elokim es</em> &mdash; the final letters spell <em>emes</em>, with which heaven and earth were sealed. For the Holy One, Blessed is He, is the very essence of truth, and the seal of the Holy One, Blessed is He, is truth. And the essential longing of Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> is only truth. And the entire Creation, from beginning to end, was only for this: to reveal the truth. As is found in the holy Zohar, that the Creation was <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;in order that they should know Him&rdquo;</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of truth. That is, for this Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> created the entire Creation: so that they should recognize and know the truth of His G-dliness and His sovereignty and His greatness etc.
</p>

<p>
And behold, the essential purpose is that they should reach the ultimate truth to its truth; that is, that we should recognize and know His truth as it truly is. For Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> is the very essence of truth, <span class="aramaic">kivyachol</span> [as it were], as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And Hashem <em>Elokim</em> is truth&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Jeremiah 10:10)</span>. So may we merit, even in this lowly world, to know the truth of His G-dliness as it truly is. And this is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;the two great luminaries&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that initially He wanted both to be great; that is, that the light of truth clothed in this world, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>, the aspect of the moon, should be equal to the very essence of the light of truth, which is Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> Himself, <span class="aramaic">kivyachol</span> &mdash; that we should merit, even in the worlds, to know His truth as it truly is, as above.
</p>

<p>
But because of the complaint of the moon &mdash; <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;it is impossible for two kings to use one crown&rdquo;</span> &mdash; for in the worlds it is impossible to bear and receive the very essence of the light of truth, for they would be nullified from existence. Therefore Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> said to her: <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;Go and diminish yourself.&rdquo;</span> And the diminution of the moon is the aspect of darkness, for its light was darkened and diminished. That is, <span class="aramaic">kivyachol</span>, Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> contracted the light of truth and hid and concealed and clothed the light of truth and diminished it, in a manner that we could receive it.
</p>

<p>
And because He diminished and contracted the light of truth &mdash; which is the aspect of the diminution of the light of the moon &mdash; from there derives the hold of the entire <span class="key-term">Sitra Achara</span>, which is the aspect of darkness, the aspect of falsehood, whose hold derives from the diminution of the light of the moon; that is, from the diminution and contraction of truth, from which derives the essential hold of falsehood, which is the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achara</span>. For certainly, if there were only the very essence of the light of truth by itself, certainly the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achara</span> &mdash; which is falsehood &mdash; would have no hold at all. For since everyone would know the very essence of truth, how would it be possible to cover the truth and turn truth into falsehood? For certainly, whoever knows the truth to its truth, it is impossible to mislead him with any falsehood in the world.
</p>

<p>
But since the truth was diminished and contracted &mdash; even though it is still complete truth &mdash; nevertheless, since the truth was diminished and covered and concealed through many contractions and garments, through this their hold unfolds. For since one does not know the very essence of truth, but rather sees the truth from afar, through many windows and garments &mdash; even though one knows the truth to its truth &mdash; nevertheless, they already have a hold, and they are able to mislead and to cover the truth with falsehood and to overturn the words of the Living G-d, to turn falsehood into truth, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>. And therefore our essential service and toil is to fill the blemish of the moon; that is, to clarify the truth from the falsehood.
</p>

<!-- ====== OS 8 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 8</div>

<p>
And therefore the essential counsel and remedy in the totality of the service that we need in this world &mdash; the essential thing is only truth. We need not to deceive ourselves, G-d forbid, but rather to look at everything with the truth to its truth, and to exert oneself in prayer &mdash; even if one cannot pray at all, at the very least one should see to it that he brings forth the utterance from his mouth in truth, according to his level. And even though the truth is not yet refined and pure, nevertheless, since he desires the truth and draws himself only toward the truth and compels himself to speak a word of truth &mdash; therefore this word of truth, even though it is not the very essence of truth, the aspect of a precious stone &mdash; even so, the truth is the aspect of a window, and another can illuminate through it. That is, the <span class="key-term">tzadikim</span> <span class="key-term-def">[righteous ones]</span> of truth, who are comprised of all the prayers of Yisroel &mdash; and to them we connect all our prayers &mdash; for the true tzadikim are, relative to us, the aspect of the very essence of truth. And they illuminate in all the prayers of Yisroel and elevate them according to the truth that is in each and every prayer of each and every person, which is the aspect of a window that receives the light from the tzadik. And according to the clarity and purity of the window &mdash; that is, the word of truth &mdash; so does the tzadik, who is the very essence of truth, illuminate within it.
</p>

<p>
And this is what is explained there in the aforementioned teaching, that one needs to connect all prayers to the tzadik of the generation etc., see there and understand well. For the tzadik of the generation together with all of Yisroel are the aspect of sun and moon, which is the aspect of Yaakov and his sons &mdash; who are the totality of the rectification of prayer, as is explained there. For Yaakov is comprised of all the twelve tribes, who are the totality of Yisroel, the totality of the twelve gates, the twelve formulations of prayer. And he [the tzadik / Yaakov] clarifies and elevates each prayer to its root, to the gate that pertains to it. For Yaakov is the aspect of the very essence of truth, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Give truth to Yaakov&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Michah 7:20)</span>. And he is the aspect of the sun, as Rabbainu of blessed memory wrote in another place, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And the sun shone upon him&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 32:32)</span>.
</p>

<p>
And the totality of Yisroel, who are the aspect of the twelve tribes, twelve gates, twelve formulations of prayer &mdash; this is the aspect of the moon, the aspect of the window mentioned above. For the moon is comprised of twelve months, for all the twelve months are reckoned to the moon, as is brought &mdash; and they correspond to the twelve tribes, the twelve formulations of prayer, the twelve gates of Yerushalayim below and above, through which prayer ascends.
</p>

<p>
And this is the aspect of the twelve <span class="key-term">windows</span> of the synagogue, which is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;and windows were open for him in his upper chamber&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Daniel 6:11)</span> &mdash; the aspect of prayer that ascends through twelve gates, which are twelve windows in the firmament through which prayer ascends. This is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;gazing through the windows&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">(Song of Songs 2:9)</span>, concerning which it is said: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;<em>chalu na</em> p&rsquo;nay El&rdquo;</span> <span class="key-term-def">[&ldquo;Entreat the face of G-d&rdquo; &mdash; where <em>chalu</em> shares the root of <em>chalon</em>, window]</span>, as is found in the Tikkunim. For prayer is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>, the aspect of the moon, as is known &mdash; the aspect of a window, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;a prayer of the poor man&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 102:1)</span>. For a poor man <span class="aramaic">leis lei mi&rsquo;garmeih klum</span> <span class="key-term-def">[has nothing of his own]</span> except what he receives from another &mdash; and this is the aspect of the moon, as above.
</p>

